  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">The Integrated Services Digital Network (ISDN) Q.921-User Adaptation
Layer (IUA) protocol, described in <xref target="RFC3057" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3057"/>, does not define a
Terminal Endpoint Identifier (TEI) Query Request message.  The
Digital Private Network Signaling System (DPNSS)/Digital Access
Signaling System 2 (DASS 2) Extensions (DUA) to the IUA Protocol,
described in <xref target="RFC4129" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4129"/>, introduces Data Link Connection (DLC) Status
messages of type 5, 6, and 7.  Then, <xref target="RFC4233" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4233"/> was published, which
updates <xref target="RFC3057" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3057"/>.  <xref target="RFC4233" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4233"/> also introduces the TEI Query Request
message and uses the message type of 5 for it.  This makes it
impossible to differentiate the DLC Status request from a TEI Query
Request.</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-2">This document updates <xref target="RFC4233" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4233"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="conventions-used-in-this-document" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2">
      <name slugifiedName="name-conventions-used-in-this-document">Conventions Used in This Document</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-2-1">The key words &quot;<bcp14>MUST</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MUST NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>REQUIRED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHALL NOT</bcp14>&quot;,
&quot;<bcp14>SHOULD</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>SHOULD NOT</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>RECOMMENDED</bcp14>&quot;, &quot;<bcp14>MAY</bcp14>&quot;, and &quot;<bcp14>OPTIONAL</bcp14>&quot; in this
document are to be interpreted as described in <xref target="RFC2119" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2119"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="new-message-type-of-the-tei-query-message" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-3">
      <name slugifiedName="name-new-message-type-of-the-tei-query-message">New Message Type of the TEI Query Message</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-1">This document updates <xref target="RFC4233" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4233"/> by introducing the following change:</t>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-3-2">Terminal Endpoint Identifier (TEI) Query messages <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> be encoded
with a message type of 8 instead of 5 as described in <xref target="RFC4233" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4233"/>.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="iana-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-4">
      <name slugifiedName="name-iana-considerations">IANA Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-4-1">In the &quot;Message Types&quot; section of the &quot;Signaling User Adaptation
Layer Assignments&quot; registry, IANA has reserved the message type 8 of
Management Messages for Terminal Endpoint Identifier (TEI) Query
Request messages.</t>
    </section>
    <section anchor="security-considerations" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-5">
      <name slugifiedName="name-security-considerations">Security Considerations</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-5-1">This document does not require any security considerations in
addition to the ones given in <xref target="RFC4233" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC4233"/>.</t>
    </section>
